.TH SCHCHECK 1
.SH NAME
schcheck \- check a netlist for what a schematic leaves undone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B schcheck
[
.I file.nl
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Schcheck
reads a netlist,
.IR netlist (5),
from the file or stdin, as
.IR schnet (1)
writes it, and tells each fault on a line:
a pin on no net (pin REF.PIN \-), unless the source marks it
unconnected on purpose (nc, pin REF.PIN nc);
a net of one pin alone;
a part of two pins or more with all of them on one net, a part
shorted.
It reads nothing but the netlist.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
schnet sheet.sch | schcheck
schcheck out/sheet.nl
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
schnet(1), netlist(5), sch(5)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
FILE: and the fault (stdin: for none), as
.PP
.RS
.nf
sheet.nl: R101.2 is on no net, and not marked nc
sheet.nl: net N has one pin alone, R101.1
sheet.nl: C102 has all its pins on net GND
.fi
.RE
.PP
Exit status 1 on a fault, 2 if the file cannot be read.
